TWC Nine End Season Play
Texas Western’s Miners put the wraps on their first baseball season at Hugo-Myer Field Wednesday afternoon by hosting the
New Mexico State Aggies in a doubleheader. Game time is 1 p.m.
Coach Andy Cohen's Miners will be gunning for wins No. 18 and No. 19 on the season. The Miners ran their season record to
17-13 over the weekend by taking one of a three-game series from potent Sul Ross.
This will be the second meeting of the season between the Miners and Aggies. In the previious engagement at Las Cruces, the two teams split a doubleheader and
set the stage for the finale Wednesday.
In the first season of competition, Cohen has done a tremendous coaching job. He molded a schools — into a top notch outfit
which displayed good power and defense.
During the 30 games to date, the Miners have whipped up 31 twin-killings. The double play combination of shortstop Jackie
Harris, second baseman Joe Carrasco and first bi an Jay Christopher has fi: greatly into the rally-nipping machine.
Christopher has been involved in 23 of the 31 double plays while Carrasco has appeared in 22 and Harris in 20.
Christopher and Nolan (Sweet Sam) Richardson lead the team in home runs with five each.
Richardson, a great all-around athlete, paces the team in runs batted in with 31, an average of better than one per game. The
strongboy has been a very valuable man for Cohen and his assistant Orville Kruschwitz. The lefty has played the outfield, first
base and toed the pitching rubber this season. He reported late for baseball because of the basketball season. He lettered three
seasons for the Miner basketball team and was the second man in the school’s history to score over 1,000 points.
Outfielder John Jimerson and catcher Charles Pearce are next in line in the RBI department with 25 each. Christopher has driven in 22 runs.
Jimerson also leads the team in hits with 39 in 96 appearances.


